g a dark theme and centering the \"Hello World\" text. The <code>body</code> element is styled with a dark background color (#333), light text color (#fff), and sans-serif font. Flexbox is used to center the content both horizontally and vertically.</p>\n\n    <h3>CSS Code:</h3>\n    <pre>\n        <code>\nbody {\n    background-color: #333;\n    color: #fff;\n    font-family: sans-serif;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: center;\n    align-items: center;\n    height: 100vh;\n    margin: 0;\n}\nh1 {\n    text-align: center;\n}\n        </code>\n    </pre>\n\n    <h2>\ud83c\udf11 Dark Theme Enhancements</h2>\n    <p>Additional CSS rules enhance the dark theme by providing specific styles for headings and links. This ensures a consistent dark theme across different HTML elements.</p>\n\n    <h3>Enhanced CSS Code:</h3>\n    <pre>\n        <code>\nbody {\n    background-color: #333;\n    color: #ddd;\n}\n\nh1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {\n    color: white;\n}\n\na {\n    color: #80cbc4; /* Teal 200 */\n}\n\na:hover {\n    color: #26a69a; /* Teal 400 */\n}\n/* Add more styles as needed */\n        </code>\n    </pre>\n\n    <h2>\ud83d\udca1 Potential Improvements</h2>\n    <p>While the current implementation fulfills the basic requirements, several improvements can be made:</p>\n    <ul>\n        <li><strong>External CSS:</strong> Moving the CSS code to an external file (e.g., <code>dark_theme.css</code>) promotes better organization and reusability.</li>\n        <li><strong>CSS Variables:</strong> Using CSS variables (custom properties) can make it easier to manage and modify the theme colors.</li>\n        <li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Adding media queries to adjust the styling for different screen sizes ensures a better user experience on various devices.</li>\n        <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Ensuring sufficient contrast between text and background colors to meet accessibility standards.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2>\ud83d\udcc1 Integration of External CSS</h2>\n    <p>To integrate the CSS from an external file, the following changes are necessary:</p>\n    <ol>\n        <li>Create a file named <code>dark_theme.css</code> and paste the CSS code into it.</li>\n        <li>Link the CSS file in the HTML <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section using the <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> tag.</li>\n    </ol>\n\n    <h3>Updated HTML Head Section:</h3>\n    <pre>\n        <code>\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=\"UTF-8\"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Hello World&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"dark_theme.css\"&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n        </code>\n    </pre>\n\n    <h2>\u2728 Final Code</h2>\n    <h3>Final HTML Code:</h3>\n    <pre>\n        <code>\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=\"en\"&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=\"UTF-8\"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Hello World&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"dark_theme.css\"&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;Hello World&lt;/h1&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n        </code>\n    </pre>\n\n    <h3>Final CSS Code (dark_theme.css):</h3>\n    <pre>\n        <code>\nbody {\n    background-color: #333;\n    color: #ddd;\n    font-family: sans-serif;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: center;\n    align-items: center;\n    height: 100vh;\n    margin: 0;\n}\n\nh1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {\n    color: white;\n    text-align: center;\n}\n\na {\n    color: #80cbc4; /* Teal 200 */\n}\n\na:hover {\n    color: #26a69a; /* Teal 400 */\n}\n/* Add more styles as needed */\n        </code>\n    </pre>\n\n\n    <h2>\ud83c\udf1f Summary</h2>\n    <p>In summary, this report provides a comprehensive overview of the \"Hello World\" web application with a dark theme. It details the HTML structure, CSS styling, potential improvements, and the integration of external CSS for better code organization and reusability. The final code ensures a clean, visually appealing, and maintainable application.</p>\n</div>",
